        "text": "Scalping is definitely not a beginner's strategy. An in depth understanding of the markets, their mechanisms, and technical analysis is needed to succeed in scalping. That said, for traders that know what they're doing, identifying the correct patterns and taking advantage of short term fluctuations can be highly profitable. If that sounds too complicated for you and you're looking for the least time involvement in your trading strategy, buy and hold is probably your best bet. It involves buying and holding an asset over a long period. It's a long term passive play where you purchase an asset and leave it alone regardless of market conditions. This strategy is known in the crypto sphere as hodling. Investors can buy and hold a coin or token for years instead of actively trading. This is a great approach for someone that prefers to be hands off and not worry about short term fluctuations.",
